# The checks of the root file, with one more disabled, and why:
# - cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg: libobs logs through blog(), a C variadic
#   function, and the glue has no other way to log. GCC and Clang check its arguments
#   against the format string; MSVC does not, as libobs's PRINTFATTR is empty there.
#   The one snprintf fills an output's error message for libobs and is checked the
#   same way. Any other C variadic call under src/obs passes unflagged as well, so it
#   needs a look in review.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg
